    <div class="snaprow">
      <figure><img src="/meowdoku-guide/board-level1.jpg" alt="Meowdoku Level 1 board, 4×4, official in-game screenshot" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Level 1 · 4×4</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/meowdoku-guide/board-level2.jpg" alt="Meowdoku Level 2 board, 4×4, official in-game screenshot" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Level 2 · 4×4</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/meowdoku-guide/board-level3.jpg" alt="Meowdoku Level 3 board, 5×5, official in-game screenshot" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Level 3 · 5×5</figcaption></figure>
    </div>


    <h2>How This Guide Compares</h2>
    <p>Meowdoku coverage online splits into three camps — and only one of them describes the game you are actually playing.</p>
    <table class="cmp">
      <thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>What you get</th><th>Watch out for</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>This guide</th><td>The real rules (cat placement, not Sudoku), Level 1–3 answers verified cell by cell with a uniqueness solver, and official board screenshots.</td><td>—</td></tr>
